that's a very valid point, specially when comparing entries with different number formats, e.g. long/double which might be equals when promoted but have different hashcode, e.g. I'm thinking off:

```
if (isWholeNumber(n1) && isDecimalNumber(n2) ||
      isDecimalNumber(n1) && isWholeNumber(n2)) {
      // if its either integer or long and the other is float or double or vice versa,
      // compare as floating point double
      return n1.doubleValue() == n2.doubleValue();
    }
```
